      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Came to the canny to suggest this same thing. It's frustrating that I can't make use of these new options because I don't want the tooltips to go away.\n\nI understand that it's not always best to introduce separate options and toggles for every possible function, but I really think these interactive objects settings should be reworked to allow for better customization. Though, it's worth pointing out though that a \"tooltip only\" option might not be sufficient for some, as they might want the combination of only tooltips and outlines, etc.\n\nFor the most range in customization without introducing too many separate options, I believe the options should be formatted like so, allowing for tooltips to be toggled separately from the other interaction effect presets:\n\n```\n\nUI Tooltips - [Off/On]\n\nInteractive Object Tooltips - [Off/On]\n\nInteractive Object Effects - [Outline, Tether line, Controller]\n\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-30T05:39:53.885Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "1. Open settings\n\n2. Go to User Interfaces\n\n3. Change Interactive Object Tooltipsm to \"Tooltip\"\n\nExpected Behavior: Tether and Highlight are hidden, Only Tooltip is visible\n\nActusl Result: Tether, Highlight, and Tooltip are shown.\n\nHaving an option to only show the tooltip would help to view names of objects/info without the distracting screen elements of the outline and tether.",
